   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "417e0659cfc6e4d8fbdfe0aee1f325d52447db3f"
   },
   "harm": "IPC Cap'n Proto serialization only overwrote a local copy, failing to write CAmount values into the message and resulting in zeroed output.",
   "hash": "28df3248bd235630",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:00+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3396163565",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3396163565",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Current code gets a local copy, overrides the local copy and local copy gets destroyed at the end of the function. Nothing is written back to the Cap'n Proto message.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-06-12",
    "by": "janb84",
    "id": "rc:3401837725",
    "quote": "yeah test was for proving the bug not the intention to add it so i'm glad you altered it somewhat !"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35511#discussion_r3396163565"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-06-18",
   "author": "optout21",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4741612688"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "417e0659cfc6e4d8fbdfe0aee1f325d52447db3f"
   },
   "harm": "Restricting construction to literals and forbidding direct integer comparison causes friction and hinders migration across the codebase.",
   "hash": "a203723c56021421",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:00+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4740188131",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4740188131",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "However, to be constructible only from `_sats` literals, and to be comparable only against other `CAmount` seems a bit of an overkill to me, and it hinders introduction (large change).",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-06-18",
    "by": "hodlinator",
    "id": "c:4741612688",
    "quote": "I briefly experimented with having an operator int64_t() method and allowing comparisons against integers. What I ran into a lot was that the compiler couldn't resolve the resulting ambiguities."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35511#issuecomment-4740188131"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-22",
   "author": "purpleKarrot",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4809818861"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "417e0659cfc6e4d8fbdfe0aee1f325d52447db3f"
   },
   "harm": "User-defined literals for amount units have known pitfalls and deviate from emerging C++ quantity standards that prefer unit multiplication syntax.",
   "hash": "9d3ced82cb684927",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:00+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4765530904",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4765530904",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Which is absolutely true and convinces me to vote against a `_sat` UDL.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-08-25",
    "by": "hodlinator",
    "id": "c:5407105124",
    "quote": "Latest push removes the `_sats` UDL. Instead the commits get by on `CAmount{<literal>}` until the end, when a `sats` unit is defined and applied as `<literal>*sats`."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35511#issuecomment-4765530904"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-29",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [
    "r:4599764409"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Transitioning the entire codebase to the new CAmount class in a single monolithic PR is too risky and onerous to review compared to an incremental rollout.",
   "hash": "5890880a7d7220ec",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:00+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:4475868693",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:4475868693",
   "kind": "scope",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "As mentioned by others, I am also not comfortable with taking such a large change in one step. I would prefer introducing a new amount type first, with a few focused examples, and then converting call sites gradually.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35511#pullrequestreview-4475868693"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-29",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3505561954"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "417e0659cfc6e4d8fbdfe0aee1f325d52447db3f"
   },
   "harm": "Placing CAmount serialization outside the class in serialize.h breaks type encapsulation.",
   "hash": "457d4b2b43d945f5",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:00+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3494097004",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3494097004",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Could we rather encapsulate the serialization inside the new type?",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-07-01",
    "by": "hodlinator",
    "id": "rc:3505561954",
    "quote": "Agreed, thanks for pushing back on this. (Edit: Fixed in later push)."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35511#discussion_r3494097004"
  }
 ],
